# What `docker build` may see (the "build context"). Allowlist: ignore everything,
# then let through only what building the app needs. Nothing else, such as a
# local .env.local with secrets, can end up in an image by accident.
#
# If the build starts importing a new top-level folder, add it here, or the
# image build fails with "file not found".
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!index.html
!.env.production
!vite.config.ts
!buildInfoPlugin.ts
!tsconfig*.json
!tailwind.config.js
!postcss.config.js
!nginx.conf
!nginx-engine-key.envsh
!src/
!public/
!icons/

# Never needed, even inside allowed folders.
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
